  }

  for (var j = 0; j < checklists.length; j++) {
    if (!checklists[j].getAssignee()) {
      context.addErrorMessage("Please assign a user to complete checklist item '" + checklists[j].getName() + "'.");
      return false;
    } else if (!checklists[j].getStatus().name.equals("Done")) {
      context.addErrorMessage("Checklist item '" + checklists[j].getName() + "' needs to be marked as 'Done' before continuing.");
      return false;
    }
  }

  return true;
}
```

6. Save the validation rule and test it out by transitioning an issue through the workflow. If all items in the linked subtasks have been completed, the issue will be allowed to move to the next column. Otherwise, it will display error messages specifying which items still need to be completed.

Note: This script assumes that you are linking subtasks using the "com.atlassian.jira.plugin.system.subtask-link" issue relation type. Adjust the code accordingly if you use a different relation type or if you want to block transitions based on other criteria.

