How can I efficiently find the unique words in Text1 that do not appear in Text2 using MATLAB? Also, can you provide a solution that can handle a large amount of text? 
Here's an implementation in MATLAB that can handle large text:
text1 = fileread('Text1.txt'); %read text1 from file
text2 = fileread('Text2.txt'); %read text2 from file
%Convert text to lowercase and split into words
words1 = lower(strsplit(text1));
words2 = lower(strsplit(text2));
%Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);
%Print the unique words
disp(uniqueWords);

response:
To make the function more efficient for handling large amounts of text, we can use memory-mapped files instead of reading the entire contents into memory at once. Here's how to modify the code:

```matlab
function uniqueWords = findUniqueWords(text1File, text2File)
    % Load the text data as memory-mapped files
    mmtext1 = mmread(text1File);
    mmtext2 = mmread(text2File);

    % Convert text to lowercase and split into words
    words1 = strsplit(lower(mmtext1(:)), ' ');
    words2 = strsplit(lower(mmtext2(:)), ' ');

    % Find unique words in text1 that do not appear in text2
    uniqueWords = setdiff(words1, words2);

    % Close the memory-mapped files
    mmclose(mmtext1);
    mmclose(mmtext2);
end
```

The `mmread()` function reads the file content into memory-mapped files, which allows us to access it without loading the entire file into RAM. This is particularly useful when dealing with very large text files that may not fit into memory. The `mmclose()` function closes the memory-mapped files after processing, freeing up system resources.

Note that memory-mapping is only supported on operating systems that support this feature (e.g., Windows, macOS). On Linux, you can use the `mmap()` function instead to achieve similar results.

