1. Firstly, you need to install the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` package via NuGet. This package provides the necessary classes for working with JWT tokens in .NET Core and .NET Framework.

2. In your WebAPI project, create an interface named `IJwtAuthenticationManager`. This interface will contain a method named `GetUsernameFromToken`, which will return the username extracted from the JWT token.

```csharp
public interface IJwtAuthenticationManager
{
