Auth0 Single Sign-On (SSO) allows you to easily manage user authentication and authorization across multiple React applications by providing a centralized login experience. With Auth0 SSO, users can sign in once and seamlessly access all your React apps without having to re-enter their credentials each time they switch between them.

Here's how you can implement Auth0 SSO for multiple React apps:

1. Create an Auth0 account and create a new application. During the setup process, select "Single Page App" as the application type and configure your application settings accordingly.

2. Install the `@auth0/auth0-spa-js` library in each of your React apps using npm or yarn. This library provides client-side authentication and authorization functionality using Auth0's REST APIs.

3. Configure each app with the same Auth0 domain and client ID. You can do this by creating a `.env` file in each app with the following variables:

```
AUTH0_DOMAIN=<your-auth0-domain>
AUTH0_CLIENT_ID=<your-auth0-client-id>
```

4. In your app's main component or entry point, initialize the Auth0 client with your domain and client ID:

```jsx
import auth0 from '@auth0/auth0-spa-js';

